// ============================================================================
// Patient: Alex Chen - Tutorial Patient
// Diagnosis: Generalized Anxiety Disorder (GAD)
// Phase: Turn 1 - Initial Introduction & Assessment
// 
// Alex is a 28-year-old marketing professional who has been struggling with
// overwhelming anxiety for the past two years. They present as put-together
// on the surface but are barely holding it together underneath. This is their
// first time seeking therapy, and they're skeptical but desperate.
//
// Key Symptoms to Discover:
// - Chronic insomnia (contradicts "sleeping fine")
// - Racing thoughts (especially at night)
// - Physical tension (shoulders, jaw clenching)
// - Avoidance behaviors (social isolation)
// - Perfectionism rooted in childhood pressure
// - Catastrophic thinking patterns
// ============================================================================

// ===========================================
// OPENING SEQUENCE - First Impressions
// ===========================================

=== START ===
NARRATOR
*Alex walks in hesitantly, clutching a coffee cup with both hands. 
They glance around the office before sitting on the edge of the chair, 
as if ready to bolt at any moment.*

@pause 2

PATIENT (nervous)
"Thanks for... seeing me, doctor."

PATIENT
"I almost didn't come today, actually."

@pause 1

PATIENT (hesitant)
"I've never done this before. Therapy, I mean."

@if rapport >= 40
    PATIENT (nervous)
    "I'm not really sure how this works."
@else
    PATIENT (guarded)
    "So... what do we do? Just talk?"
@endif

-> worry_intro

=== worry_intro ===
NARRATOR
*Alex takes a long sip of coffee, avoiding eye contact.*

@pause 1.5

PATIENT (anxious)
"I just... I [can't stop worrying about everything]."

PATIENT
"Work, my family, money, my health..."

PATIENT (stressed)
"Even [little things] like whether I locked the door or turned off the stove."

@pause 1

PATIENT (embarrassed)
"Sometimes I go back three or four times to check."

-> sleep_topic

=== sleep_topic ===
NARRATOR
*You notice dark circles under Alex's eyes that their concealer 
can't quite hide.*

@pause 1

@if rapport >= 60
    PATIENT (hesitant)
    "And my sleep... it's been [okay, I guess]<contradicts:bags-under-eyes>."
    
    PATIENT
    "I mean, who sleeps great these days, right?"
@elseif rapport >= 40
    PATIENT (defensive)
    "Sleep? I'm [sleeping fine, really]<contradicts:bags-under-eyes>."
    
    PATIENT
    "Just tired from work. That's normal."
@else
    PATIENT (guarded)
    "[My sleep is fine]<contradicts:bags-under-eyes>. That's not why I'm here."
@endif

PATIENT
"Anyway, I just wanted to... I don't know. Talk to someone, I guess."

@pause 0.5

PATIENT (nervous)
"Is that enough of a reason to be here?"

// ===========================================
// RESPONSE HANDLERS - Core Topics
// ===========================================

// -------------------------------------------
// FAMILY - Parents & Upbringing
// -------------------------------------------

=== @response:family.parents ===
NARRATOR
*Alex's posture stiffens slightly at the mention of parents.*

@pause 0.5

@if rapport >= 75
    PATIENT (thoughtful)
    "My parents... they [mean well], I think."
    
    @pause 1
    
    PATIENT (sad)
    "They've always [expected a lot from me]. Always."
    
    PATIENT
    "Good grades, good school, good job, good life..."
    
    PATIENT (vulnerable)
    "But no matter what I achieve, there's always something more."
    
    @pause 0.5
    
    PATIENT (sad)
    "I don't think I've ever quite [measured up] in their eyes."
    
    @reveal parental-pressure
    @rapport +8
    
@elseif rapport >= 55
    PATIENT (hesitant)
    "They're... supportive, I guess. In their way."
    
    PATIENT
    "We talk sometimes. Not about anything real though."
    
    @pause 0.5
    
    PATIENT (deflecting)
    "They live across the country now, so..."
    
    @rapport +3
    
@else
    PATIENT (guarded)
    "I'd rather not talk about my parents right now."
    
    PATIENT (defensive)
    "They're not why I'm here. Can we focus on something else?"
    
    @rapport -2
@endif

=== @response:family.childhood ===
NARRATOR
*Alex looks down at their coffee cup, slowly rotating it in their hands.*

@pause 1

@if rapport >= 80
    PATIENT (vulnerable)
    "My childhood was... complicated."
    
    @pause 1.5
    
    PATIENT (sad)
    "I always felt like I had to be [perfect] to be loved."
    
    PATIENT
    "Perfect grades. Perfect behavior. Never cause any problems."
    
    PATIENT (thoughtful)
    "I remember being seven and crying because I got a 95 on a test."
    
    @pause 0.5
    
    PATIENT (sad)
    "Because I knew my parents would ask why I missed those five points."
    
    PATIENT (vulnerable)
    "That pressure... it [never really went away]."
    
    @reveal childhood-anxiety
    @reveal perfectionism-origin
    @rapport +12
    @set revealed_childhood = true
    
@elseif rapport >= 60
    PATIENT (hesitant)
    "It was... normal, I suppose."
    
    PATIENT
    "Good family, good schools, all that."
    
    @pause 0.5
    
    PATIENT (deflecting)
    "Nothing special to report, really."
    
    PATIENT (guarded)
    "Why does everyone always want to talk about childhood?"
    
    @rapport +2
    
@else
    PATIENT (defensive)
    "Why do you need to know about that?"
    
    PATIENT (frustrated)
    "I'm not here to dig through ancient history."
    
    PATIENT
    "Can we please focus on the present?"
    
    @rapport -5
@endif

=== @response:family.siblings ===
@if rapport >= 50
    PATIENT (thoughtful)
    "I have a younger sister. Sarah."
    
    @pause 0.5
    
    PATIENT (sad)
    "She's... different from me. More carefree, I guess."
    
    @if rapport >= 70
        PATIENT (vulnerable)
        "Sometimes I [envy her]. She doesn't seem to worry about anything."
        
        PATIENT
        "Or maybe she's just better at hiding it."
        
        @rapport +5
    @else
        PATIENT
        "We're not super close anymore."
    @endif
@else
    PATIENT (guarded)
    "I have a sister. We don't really talk much."
@endif

// -------------------------------------------
// WORK - Job & Career Stress
// -------------------------------------------

=== @response:work.job ===
PATIENT
"I work in marketing. Digital marketing, specifically."

@pause 0.5

PATIENT
"Mid-level position at a tech company. It's... fine."

@if rapport >= 65
    PATIENT (stressed)
    "The [deadlines are constant]. There's always another campaign."
    
    PATIENT
    "Another presentation. Another crisis."
    
    PATIENT (anxious)
    "I'm always worried I'll [miss something important]."
    
    @pause 0.5
    
    PATIENT (stressed)
    "Or that someone will finally figure out I don't belong there."
    
    @rapport +5
    @reveal impostor-feelings
    
@elseif rapport >= 45
    PATIENT
    "It pays well. Good benefits."
    
    PATIENT (deflecting)
    "Can't complain, really."
@else
    PATIENT (guarded)
    "It's just a job. Pays the bills."
@endif

=== @response:work.stress ===
NARRATOR
*Alex's grip tightens on the coffee cup.*

@pause 0.5

@if rapport >= 70
    PATIENT (stressed)
    "The stress is... [constant]. Relentless."
    
    PATIENT
    "I wake up thinking about work. I go to sleep thinking about work."
    
    @pause 1
    
    PATIENT (anxious)
    "Sometimes I feel like I'm [drowning] and no one even notices."
    
    PATIENT (vulnerable)
    "Like I'm screaming underwater."
    
    @pause 0.5
    
    PATIENT (sad)
    "I used to love my job. Now I [dread going in] every morning."
    
    @rapport +8
    @reveal work-anxiety
    @set admitted_work_stress = true
    
@elseif rapport >= 50
    PATIENT (hesitant)
    "Work stress? I mean, it's a demanding job."
    
    PATIENT
    "But that's just how it is, isn't it?"
    
    PATIENT (deflecting)
    "Everyone deals with work stress."
    
    @rapport +2
    
@else
    PATIENT (dismissive)
    "Work is work. Stress comes with the territory."
    
    PATIENT
    "I handle it fine."
@endif

=== @response:work.performance ===
@if rapport >= 60
    PATIENT (anxious)
    "My performance? I... I worry about it constantly."
    
    PATIENT
    "Every email from my boss makes my [heart race]."
    
    @pause 0.5
    
    PATIENT (stressed)
    "I [triple-check everything] before submitting."
    
    PATIENT
    "Sometimes I stay late just to review my work again and again."
    
    @if rapport >= 75
        PATIENT (vulnerable)
        "It's never good enough. *I'm* never good enough."
        
        @rapport +10
        @reveal perfectionism-work
    @else
        @rapport +5
    @endif
@else
    PATIENT (guarded)
    "My work is fine. I do my job."
    
    PATIENT
    "Why are you asking about that?"
@endif

=== @response:work.colleagues ===
@if rapport >= 55
    PATIENT (thoughtful)
    "My coworkers? They're... fine, I guess."
    
    @pause 0.5
    
    PATIENT (hesitant)
    "I don't really [connect with them] though."
    
    PATIENT
    "Everyone seems to have their groups, their inside jokes..."
    
    @if rapport >= 70
        PATIENT (sad)
        "I eat lunch at my desk most days. Alone."
        
        PATIENT (deflecting)
        "It's easier that way. Less exhausting."
        
        @rapport +5
        @reveal social-withdrawal-work
    @endif
@else
    PATIENT
    "We get along fine. Professional."
@endif

// -------------------------------------------
// EMOTIONS - Anxiety & Mood
// -------------------------------------------

=== @response:emotions.anxiety ===
NARRATOR
*Alex pauses, seeming to consider the question carefully.*

@pause 1.5

@if rapport >= 75
    PATIENT (vulnerable)
    "Anxiety... yeah. That's probably the right word."
    
    @pause 1
    
    PATIENT
    "It feels like there's always a [weight on my chest]."
    
    PATIENT (anxious)
    "Like something bad is about to happen, even when everything's fine."
    
    PATIENT
    "Especially when everything's fine, actually."
    
    @pause 0.5
    
    PATIENT (sad)
    "Because that's when I'm waiting for the other shoe to drop."
    
    @rapport +12
    @reveal anxiety-admission
    @set admitted_anxiety = true
    
@elseif rapport >= 50
    PATIENT (hesitant)
    "I get nervous sometimes. Doesn't everyone?"
    
    PATIENT
    "I wouldn't call it anxiety exactly..."
    
    @pause 0.5
    
    PATIENT (thoughtful)
    "Or maybe I just don't want to."
    
    @rapport +3
    
@else
    PATIENT (defensive)
    "I'm not anxious. I'm just stressed."
    
    PATIENT (frustrated)
    "There's a difference, isn't there?"
    
    PATIENT
    "I can handle my stress. I don't have a problem."
    
    @rapport -3
@endif

=== @response:emotions.mood ===
PATIENT (thoughtful)
"My mood? It's..."

@pause 1

@if rapport >= 60
    PATIENT (sad)
    "It's been [up and down], honestly."
    
    PATIENT
    "Some days I feel almost normal. Like myself again."
    
    @pause 0.5
    
    PATIENT (vulnerable)
    "Other days I just want to [hide under the covers] and disappear."
    
    PATIENT
    "Those days are happening more often lately."
    
    @rapport +5
    @reveal mood-fluctuation
    
@elseif rapport >= 40
    PATIENT
    "It's... okay, I guess. Normal?"
    
    PATIENT (hesitant)
    "I'm not depressed or anything, if that's what you're asking."
@else
    PATIENT (guarded)
    "Fine. My mood is fine."
@endif

=== @response:emotions.worry ===
@if rapport >= 65
    PATIENT (anxious)
    "The worrying... it never stops."
    
    PATIENT
    "It's like my brain has a [list of things to worry about]."
    
    @pause 0.5
    
    PATIENT (stressed)
    "And as soon as I check one thing off, three more appear."
    
    PATIENT
    "Did I send that email correctly? Will my car make it to work?"
    
    PATIENT (anxious)
    "What if I said something wrong in that meeting? What if they hate me?"
    
    @pause 1
    
    PATIENT (vulnerable)
    "It's [exhausting]. Living like this."
    
    @rapport +8
    @reveal racing-thoughts
    
@else
    PATIENT
    "I worry sometimes. Everyone does."
    
    PATIENT (deflecting)
    "It's not that bad."
@endif

=== @response:emotions.fear ===
@if rapport >= 70
    PATIENT (vulnerable)
    "What am I afraid of?"
    
    @pause 1.5
    
    PATIENT (thoughtful)
    "Everything? Nothing specific?"
    
    PATIENT
    "It's like this [constant hum of fear] in the background."
    
    PATIENT (anxious)
    "Fear that something will go wrong. That I'll mess up."
    
    @pause 0.5
    
    PATIENT (sad)
    "Fear that everyone will finally see that I'm [not good enough]."
    
    @rapport +10
    @reveal core-fear
    
@else
    PATIENT (guarded)
    "I'm not really afraid of anything specific."
    
    PATIENT
    "Normal stuff, I guess."
@endif

// -------------------------------------------
// SLEEP - Insomnia & Rest
// -------------------------------------------

=== @response:emotions.sleep ===
NARRATOR
*Alex's hand unconsciously moves toward the dark circles under their eyes.*

@pause 0.5

@if rapport >= 80 && has_symptom("bags-under-eyes")
    PATIENT (relieved)
    "*sighs* Okay, you can probably tell just by looking at me."
    
    @pause 1
    
    PATIENT (vulnerable)
    "I [haven't slept properly in weeks]. Maybe months."
    
    PATIENT
    "I lie awake for hours. My mind just [won't stop]."
    
    @pause 0.5
    
    PATIENT (sad)
    "Every mistake I've ever made. Everything that could go wrong tomorrow."
    
    PATIENT
    "It all plays on repeat, over and over."
    
    @pause 1
    
    PATIENT (exhausted)
    "By 3 AM, I'm [exhausted but wide awake]."
    
    PATIENT
    "Sometimes I don't fall asleep until the sun comes up."
    
    @rapport +15
    @reveal insomnia
    @reveal racing-thoughts-night
    @set admitted_sleep = true
    @unlock deep_sleep_discussion
    
@elseif rapport >= 65
    PATIENT (hesitant)
    "Sleep is... complicated."
    
    PATIENT
    "Some nights are better than others."
    
    @pause 0.5
    
    PATIENT (tired)
    "I guess I don't [sleep as well as I used to]."
    
    PATIENT
    "My brain doesn't seem to have an off switch anymore."
    
    @rapport +5
    
@elseif rapport >= 45
    PATIENT (defensive)
    "I told you, I sleep fine."
    
    PATIENT
    "Everyone has trouble sleeping sometimes."
    
    PATIENT (deflecting)
    "It's no big deal."
    
@else
    PATIENT (guarded)
    "Why do you [keep asking about that]?"
    
    PATIENT (frustrated)
    "My sleep is fine. Can we move on?"
    
    @rapport -5
@endif

=== @response:sleep.routine ===
@if rapport >= 60
    PATIENT (hesitant)
    "My sleep routine? I... don't really have one."
    
    PATIENT
    "I usually work until I can't keep my eyes open."
    
    @pause 0.5
    
    PATIENT (anxious)
    "Then I lie in bed [scrolling on my phone] for hours."
    
    PATIENT
    "Checking emails. Checking social media. Checking... everything."
    
    @if rapport >= 75
        PATIENT (vulnerable)
        "It's like I'm [afraid to be alone with my thoughts]."
        
        @rapport +8
        @reveal avoidance-behavior
    @endif
@else
    PATIENT
    "I go to bed, I wake up. Not much of a routine."
@endif

=== @response:sleep.dreams ===
@if rapport >= 70
    PATIENT (thoughtful)
    "Dreams? I... I do have nightmares sometimes."
    
    @pause 1
    
    PATIENT (anxious)
    "Usually about work. About [messing something up]."
    
    PATIENT
    "Or showing up somewhere important completely unprepared."
    
    @pause 0.5
    
    PATIENT (vulnerable)
    "I wake up in a [cold sweat], heart pounding."
    
    PATIENT
    "And then I can't fall back asleep because I'm worried it might be real."
    
    @rapport +8
    @reveal nightmare-anxiety
@else
    PATIENT
    "I don't really remember my dreams."
@endif

