// -------------------------------------------
// THERAPY - About This Process
// -------------------------------------------

=== @response:therapy.expectations ===
PATIENT (hesitant)
"What do I expect from this?"

@pause 1

@if rapport >= 55
    PATIENT (honest)
    "I don't know, honestly."
    
    PATIENT
    "I just want to feel [normal] again."
    
    @pause 0.5
    
    PATIENT (vulnerable)
    "Or maybe I've never been normal. Maybe I want to finally figure out [what's wrong with me]."
    
    @rapport +5
@else
    PATIENT
    "I'm not sure. Someone suggested I try this."
    
    PATIENT (skeptical)
    "We'll see if it helps."
@endif

=== @response:therapy.previous ===
PATIENT
"This is my first time in therapy."

@pause 0.5

@if rapport >= 50
    PATIENT (hesitant)
    "I almost went a few years ago, but..."
    
    PATIENT (embarrassed)
    "I talked myself out of it. Convinced myself I didn't need it."
    
    @if rapport >= 70
        PATIENT (sad)
        "I kept thinking 'other people have it [worse than me]'."
        
        PATIENT
        "That I should just [push through] on my own."
        
        @rapport +5
    @endif
@else
    PATIENT
    "I've never done this before."
@endif

=== @response:therapy.concerns ===
@if rapport >= 60
    PATIENT (honest)
    "I'm nervous about this. About being here."
    
    @pause 0.5
    
    PATIENT (vulnerable)
    "Part of me is [afraid you'll judge me]."
    
    PATIENT
    "That you'll think I'm weak or broken or just... pathetic."
    
    @pause 1
    
    @if rapport >= 75
        PATIENT (sad)
        "Because that's what I think about myself most days."
        
        @rapport +10
        @reveal self-judgment
    @else
        @rapport +5
    @endif
@else
    PATIENT
    "No concerns really. I'm just here to talk."
@endif

// ===========================================
// BREAKTHROUGH MOMENTS
// ===========================================

=== @breakthrough:sleep ===
@trigger keyword-sleep-lie + bags-under-eyes

NARRATOR
*Alex's eyes widen slightly as they realize the contradiction.
A flicker of something—relief? fear?—crosses their face.*

@pause 1

PATIENT (relieved)
"*sighs deeply*"

@pause 0.5

PATIENT
"Okay. Okay, you're right."

@pause 1

PATIENT (vulnerable)
"I [haven't slept properly in weeks]. Maybe longer."

PATIENT
"I lie awake for hours every night."

@pause 0.5

PATIENT (sad)
"My mind just [won't stop racing]<reveals:racing-thoughts>."

PATIENT
"Every mistake I've ever made. Everything I need to do tomorrow."

PATIENT (anxious)
"Everything that could go wrong."

@pause 1

PATIENT (exhausted)
"It all plays on repeat, over and over."

PATIENT
"By the time I finally fall asleep, it's almost time to wake up."

@pause 0.5

PATIENT (vulnerable)
"Every night I tell myself tomorrow will be different<reveals:insomnia>."

PATIENT (sad)
"But it never is."

@rapport +20
@focus +50
@reveal insomnia
@reveal racing-thoughts
@set breakthrough_sleep = true
@unlock deep_sleep_discussion

NARRATOR
*For the first time since arriving, Alex's shoulders visibly relax.
The admission, however painful, seems to lift a weight.*

-> post_breakthrough_sleep

=== post_breakthrough_sleep ===
@pause 2

PATIENT (thoughtful)
"I don't know why I said I was sleeping fine."

PATIENT (sad)
"I guess I didn't want to admit how bad it's gotten."

@pause 0.5

PATIENT (hesitant)
"Even to myself."

-> end_turn

